#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Pre-push hook: intentionally a no-op (#719).
#
# History: #571 ran the full `make test` here to keep `main` green, because the
# repo pushes straight to `main` (no PR gate). Removed 2026-07-12 (#719):
#   - the suite grew to ~3.5 min (5000+ tests) — far past #571's "runnable
#     locally in <1 minute" premise, so the per-push tax no longer pays off;
#   - `test-ci.yml` already runs the full pytest suite on `push: [main]`, so
#     code IS checked post-push by CI (an occasional briefly-red main, caught
#     by CI + fix-forward, is the accepted trade for fast pushes);
#   - doc-frontmatter — the original motivation for a local gate — is caught at
#     commit time by the `.githooks/pre-commit` gate, not here.
#
# There is deliberately no pre-push test gate now. If you want to run the suite
# before pushing, run `make test` yourself.
#
# See docs/runbooks/local-test-gate.md for the full rationale.

exit 0
